# Granular BlocBuilders

**Rule:** When a large widget depends on several different fields of the state, do not wrap the whole UI in a single `BlocBuilder` with a meaningless `buildWhen` (e.g. `previous != current`). That rebuilds the entire screen on any change. Split the UI into smaller widgets, each wrapped in its own `BlocBuilder` with a `buildWhen` that compares only the field it cares about.

### ❌ Bad Example
```dart
BlocBuilder<MyCubit, MyState>(
  buildWhen: (p, c) => p != c, // rebuilds everything
  builder: (context, state) => Column(children: [
    _tab(state.selectedTab),
    _passengers(state.passengerCount),
    _price(state.totalPrice),
  ]),
);
```

### ✅ Good Example
```dart
Column(children: [_TabSection(), _PassengerSection(), _PriceSection()]);

class _PriceSection extends StatelessWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => BlocBuilder<MyCubit, MyState>(
        buildWhen: (p, c) => p.totalPrice != c.totalPrice,
        builder: (context, state) => Text('${state.totalPrice}'),
      );
}
```
